From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erhan Bilgili <erhan.bilgili@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 13:53:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/49] winewayland: Keep input state across role rebuilds

Role teardown is not necessarily an input focus loss: Toplevels can briefly
drop and recreate their role while the same wl_surface remains alive. Keep
cached input focus and pointer constraints across role rebuilds and clear
them only when destroying the wl_surface. Compositor enter/leave events
remain responsible for live focus changes.

Fixes focus loss in Resident Evil Requiem Demo when changing display modes.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
index 14c20cb9cb8..d2db1574756 100644
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -592,6 +592,8 @@ static void wayland_surface_clear_child_surfaces(struct wayland_surface *surface
     surface->dmabuf_top = NULL;
 }
 
+/* Clear cached input state when the wl_surface is destroyed. Role changes are
+ * not input events; compositor enter/leave handles focus while the surface lives. */
 static void wayland_surface_clear_input_state(struct wayland_surface *surface)
 {
     pthread_mutex_lock(&process_wayland.pointer.mutex);
@@ -981,6 +983,7 @@ err:
  */
 void wayland_surface_destroy(struct wayland_surface *surface)
 {
+    wayland_surface_clear_input_state(surface);
     wayland_surface_clear_role(surface);
 
     if (surface->wp_alpha_modifier_surface_v1)
@@ -1517,7 +1520,7 @@ void wayland_surface_clear_role(struct wayland_surface *surface)
 {
     TRACE("surface=%p\n", surface);
 
-    wayland_surface_clear_input_state(surface);
+    /* Keep input state across role churn; it follows wl_surface enter/leave. */
     wayland_surface_clear_child_surfaces(surface);
 
     /* some objects are shared between several roles */
